id": "c168da1e-88fa-4010-957e-7ecc30a7cf42", "type": "concept", "title": "idea"}], "description": "This subtopic develops Berkeley's immaterialism and critique of matter."}, {"id": "f97e6472-01d5-4e58-a31b-c34823b4632b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "God and the order of experience", "children": [{"id": "b514d641-5345-4eab-886f-0204a422fe3a", "type": "concept", "title": "God"}, {"id": "3c116669-86cf-445f-93b1-f6185c26cb5a", "type": "concept", "title": "divine perception"}, {"id": "d21a3081-1e7d-4884-983f-f80fa310ac23", "type": "concept", "title": "laws of nature"}, {"id": "3b228884-4ed0-468b-a72a-1a943382e2b2", "type": "concept", "title": "regularity"}, {"id": "648bcef1-c1ba-4f39-a099-8e37b73dfbdf", "type": "concept", "title": "continued existence"}, {"id": "7fceba14-664f-422f-993f-fc7b5bbd8bc0", "type": "concept", "title": "finite spirit"}, {"id": "a7ccb28d-f2a9-45d8-9966-ef58655397f1", "type": "concept", "title": "passive idea"}, {"id": "086c9613-bb46-4af4-9b20-17a0224375e9", "type": "concept", "title": "active mind"}, {"id": "edcc265d-e64d-48d8-a65b-1f46f67ae032", "type": "concept", "title": "natural sign"}, {"id": "e7c5c810-7613-4770-9983-cd4a20ace4b4", "type": "concept", "title": "religious apologetics"}], "description": "Students examine how Berkeley preserves object stability and natural order without matter."}]}, {"id": "877c361a-ddc1-45d7-9c18-f84c1eb8d459", "type": "topic", "title": "Hume: Impressions, Ideas, Causation, and Induction", "description": "Explore Hume's empiricist psychology and skeptical account of causal reasoning. Explain Hume's copy principle, problem of induction, and analysis of causation as habit or custom.", "children": [{"id": "90ad5510-b684-4aa9-89e7-afc4bc6ef699", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Impressions and ideas", "children": [{"id": "163a6b6e-18ec-45ad-8337-7f614b8a13a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Treatise"}, {"id": "83f4fac2-4cb5-4de7-847e-7c3fefeca339", "type": "concept", "title": "Enquiry"}, {"id": "caed8b1c-5ef5-4748-8fcf