, "type": "subtopic", "title": "Induction and probability", "children": [{"id": "408bf751-3610-4f58-8265-41db4f652e98", "type": "concept", "title": "problem of induction"}, {"id": "08341a63-b759-4c21-a16a-a78a9bd3dbbc", "type": "concept", "title": "uniformity of nature"}, {"id": "a3d3104f-b504-43f0-8789-1264ba7e0b18", "type": "concept", "title": "demonstrative reasoning"}, {"id": "27edafc2-b626-4dc7-b779-f74ae8b707b7", "type": "concept", "title": "probable reasoning"}, {"id": "2540859f-837f-44c4-a6a7-569145961059", "type": "concept", "title": "matter of fact"}, {"id": "2867ef01-7e77-4d0c-a179-57640170a916", "type": "concept", "title": "relations of ideas"}, {"id": "6ef8ec75-7f4b-4cdf-99e9-263bea2ec1a2", "type": "concept", "title": "skeptical argument"}, {"id": "46a432ba-3288-43a2-a716-dbb930c531a4", "type": "concept", "title": "mitigated skepticism"}, {"id": "e6047247-9b3d-4326-b828-9b4c99a47644", "type": "concept", "title": "belief"}, {"id": "e3f5fa68-3fa5-4f20-8545-af4a86624379", "type": "concept", "title": "evidence"}], "description": "Students learn why Hume thinks reason cannot justify expecting the future to resemble the past."}]}, {"id": "399941a8-0f00-44c4-9caf-fe6d8afe2d75", "type": "topic", "title": "Hume: Self, Moral Sentiment, Religion, and Naturalism", "description": "Consider Hume's wider philosophical naturalism in personal identity, ethics, religion, and social life. Evaluate Hume's bundle theory, sentiment-based moral theory, critique of miracles, and naturalistic method.", "children": [{"id": "30616796-f887-4d51-8cbc-8223d872d9e5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "The self and personal identity", "children": [{"id": "b23cb315-87ce-4d78-ad9b-f8fb6a008a7b", "type": "concept", "title": "bundle theory"}, {"id": "68a0a2ce-553c-48a7-b1f3-c8715cf717c6", "type": "concept", "title": "personal identity"}, {"id": "7a44e036-cb83-4b20-a63c-f0de5e332d14", "type": "concept", "title": "perception"}, {"id": "26646975-1d9d-418f-bb10-63e61c45e05e", "type": "concept", "t