e8d1c791", "type": "concept", "title": "Damaris Masham"}, {"id": "b3fcd158-4c1f-4d75-b858-3572501d57ab", "type": "concept", "title": "mind-body objection"}, {"id": "182f20bc-159d-40f6-8ed9-af36b9987bd2", "type": "concept", "title": "education"}, {"id": "37cdc7bc-8e2e-47db-afe2-d5be8e6eabc6", "type": "concept", "title": "substance"}, {"id": "2550d185-cd0f-444b-9f1f-10aaaf7c9116", "type": "concept", "title": "natural philosophy"}], "description": "Students encounter major early modern thinkers often omitted from standard surveys."}, {"id": "5304743b-1e1c-4aa3-8762-ee4c9e963f00", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Enlightenment equality and critique", "children": [{"id": "1b9eaf94-62ef-4bf2-853d-b70f9ad93bfc", "type": "concept", "title": "Mary Wollstonecraft"}, {"id": "fd78134c-43e3-498e-bc80-ade6eac0257d", "type": "concept", "title": "Vindication of the Rights of Woman"}, {"id": "c3825a21-f585-4d78-92af-a5bdf339417d", "type": "concept", "title": "education"}, {"id": "7f8577f2-f2a3-44bc-aedc-dd86046ba016", "type": "concept", "title": "virtue"}, {"id": "278e6c1c-bada-4af5-bc9b-cb7cba6211ae", "type": "concept", "title": "dependency"}, {"id": "5a686a46-4010-455c-8ecb-5819a087ad7f", "type": "concept", "title": "reason"}, {"id": "2bc25ddb-70be-4e42-aebd-bf1115aa2777", "type": "concept", "title": "gender hierarchy"}, {"id": "541259d9-3a81-4cff-9a51-743ce882b2a2", "type": "concept", "title": "citizenship"}, {"id": "db4b615e-4bd3-4bfd-9dd9-bf2b2b5d8491", "type": "concept", "title": "public sphere"}, {"id": "4f0f4491-d4f0-466a-8d38-c8779bac78f7", "type": "concept", "title": "equality"}], "description": "This subtopic examines how modern concepts of reason and liberty were contested from within."}, {"id": "a60bcb53-05d7-4c8f-8232-45866895051e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Race, colonialism, and universal reason", "children": [{"id": "6add3101-b876-4cde-ac0d-577ce0dd1703", "type": "concept", "title": "Anton Wilhelm Amo"}, {"id": "a6805c49-373b-41a6-83d9-dcdc39088884", "type": "concept", "title": "race"}, {"id": "b5f8a57c-4cf6-4ed0-b8dd-d52b6f0679e0", "type": "concept", "title": "slavery"}, {"id": "7ddc0e75-55cd-4229-b745-4b84cbf4db9c", "type": "concept", "title": "colonialism"}, {"id": "db826310-ee4b-4053-b8a1-a026421d8500", "type": "concept", "title": "universalism"}, {"id": "48435e40-ea68-4af6-a9d2-6de63d43ab60", "type": "concept", "title": "human nature"}, {"id": "a2c58b63-f22a-4d70-9cc8-8add136ad781", "type": "concept", "title": "anthropology"}, {"id": "ad392a01-61e2-4a31-9451-b08f62c48ba6", "type": "concept", "title": "classification"}, {"id": "690c6385-7c68-4f4a-afd3-95dc9d587f05", "type": "concept", "title": "Eurocentrism"}, {"id": "d81a261d-24a9-48af-97e3-0b57b3818255", "type": "concept", "title": "exclusion"}], "description": "Students evaluate the tension between Enlightenment universalism and colonial/racial hierarchy."}]}, {"id": "c5d33f66-75ec-40f8-8138-83b89b3c89b0", "type": "topic", "title": "Rousseau and the Enlightenment Problem of Freedom", "description": "Study Rousseau's critique of modern civilization and his account of political freedom and moral development. Analyze Rousseau's relation to Enlightenment thought through inequality, authenticity, general will, and civic freedom.", "children": [{"id": "41dcbdb2-0e5c-4d37-9469-0ab8dae1a3a8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Natural human beings and inequality", "children": [{"id": "25622391-3159-42be-9f53-f703673276f1", "type": "concept", "title": "state of nature"}, {"id": "c1b6d360-9bc6-41a2-985f-9679087a3d5f", "type": "concept", "title": "amour de soi"}, {"id": "fde65b04-7ac5-4068-a8a3-46b0da0e756b", "type": "concept", "title": "amour-propre"}, {"id": "6fca3b82-6647-4f42-8540-efaf480dd932", "type": "concept", "title": "perfectibility"}, {"id": "1e791d16-cca5-4227-a283-b7339452b206", "type": "concept", "title": "pity"}, {"id": "69632b35-36f2-423c-9c57-402e69fef4bb", "type": "concept", "title": "property"}, {"id": "e8b19867-abb5-4b89-9a9b-00476465913b", "type": "concept", "titl