t"}, {"id": "c168da1e-88fa-4010-957e-7ecc30a7cf42", "type": "concept", "title": "idea"}], "description": "This subtopic develops Berkeley's immaterialism and critique of matter."}, {"id": "f97e6472-01d5-4e58-a31b-c34823b4632b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "God and the order of experience", "children": [{"id": "b514d641-5345-4eab-886f-0204a422fe3a", "type": "concept", "title": "God"}, {"id": "3c116669-86cf-445f-93b1-f6185c26cb5a", "type": "concept", "title": "divine perception"}, {"id": "d21a3081-1e7d-4884-983f-f80fa310ac23", "type": "concept", "title": "laws of nature"}, {"id": "3b228884-4ed0-468b-a72a-1a943382e2b2", "type": "concept", "title": "regularity"}, {"id": "648bcef1-c1ba-4f39-a099-8e37b73dfbdf", "type": "concept", "title": "continued existence"}, {"id": "7fceba14-664f-422f-993f-fc7b5bbd8bc0", "type": "concept", "title": "finite spirit"}, {"id": "a7ccb28d-f2a9-45d8-9966-ef58655397f1", "type": "concept", "title": "passive idea"}, {"id": "086c9613-bb46-4af4-9b20-17a0224375e9", "type": "concept", "title": "active mind"}, {"id": "edcc265d-e64d-48d8-a65b-1f46f67ae032", "type": "concept", "title": "natural sign"}, {"id": "e7c5c810-7613-4770-9983-cd4a20ace4b4", "type": "concept", "title": "religious apologetics"}], "description": "Students examine how Berkeley preserves object stability and natural order without matter."}]}, {"id": "877c361a-ddc1-45d7-9c18-f84c1eb8d459", "type": "topic", "title": "Hume: Impressions, Ideas, Causation, and Induction", "description": "Explore Hume's empiricist psychology and skeptical account of causal reasoning. Explain Hume's copy principle, problem of induction, and analysis of causation as habit or custom.", "children": [{"id": "90ad5510-b684-4aa9-89e7-afc4bc6ef699", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Impressions and ideas", "children": [{"id": "163a6b6e-18ec-45ad-8337-7f614b8a13a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Treatise"}, {"id": "83f4fac2-4cb5-4de7-847e-7c3fefeca339", "type": "concept", "title": "Enquiry"}, {"id": "caed8b1c-5ef5-4748-8fcf-9fe77ef8e59e", "type": "concept", "title": "impression"}, {"id": "20b59bb1-cf5f-4c2b-a50a-afdb1a02338b", "type": "concept", "title": "idea"}, {"id": "abbe4f41-13b6-43fe-8c2c-1912d920e734", "type": "concept", "title": "copy principle"}, {"id": "cfe54517-b967-44bf-bd1f-7b7bf8dc9940", "type": "concept", "title": "association"}, {"id": "6cc5dd7b-0e59-4528-8a43-b6f2ed4ab60f", "type": "concept", "title": "resemblance"}, {"id": "9bd19955-b327-45d1-b438-4cd27da3466a", "type": "concept", "title": "contiguity"}, {"id": "172554b2-2fcb-4879-be67-239a60fc4eae", "type": "concept", "title": "cause and effect"}, {"id": "b2186f76-1fb2-4559-b674-9bba4b266ffa", "type": "concept", "title": "vivacity"}], "description": "Students learn Hume's basic theory of mental contents and association."}, {"id": "6c53e8eb-1caf-42fb-bc3c-fee6d88deb76", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Causation and necessary connection", "children": [{"id": "7a406a06-a5db-4f5b-824d-5c1d97ce0198", "type": "concept", "title": "constant conjunction"}, {"id": "fd164b9b-ae9e-476f-a7a0-05477a7bd785", "type": "concept", "title": "necessary connection"}, {"id": "06db53cb-399a-431e-bb00-5d2798d86d40", "type": "concept", "title": "custom"}, {"id": "67a02d53-081b-4da2-8fad-1806ba8878b8", "type": "concept", "title": "habit"}, {"id": "eee674b1-d5a1-445f-be6c-4f2b5656b793", "type": "concept", "title": "causal inference"}, {"id": "db53ceff-7be9-4f57-9e69-bf2991364c96", "type": "concept", "title": "secret power"}, {"id": "13ce5edf-f686-41a9-aae2-33083de3fe78", "type": "concept", "title": "regularity"}, {"id": "04fa1637-f135-4d9d-850a-83b53373138e", "type": "concept", "title": "expectation"}, {"id": "c8dae590-f470-4c3e-b111-c0cc93a1458d", "type": "concept", "title": "natural belief"}, {"id": "03949e18-11d9-45c1-aba9-e108600eca7a", "type": "concept", "title": "skeptical solution"}], "description": "This subtopic shows Hume's challenge to rationalist and metaphysical accounts of causation."}, {"id": "be9331a5-ef2e-46af-9212-1f28d66bf379", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Induction and probability", "children": [{"id": "408bf751-3610-4f58-8265-41db4f652e98", "type": "concept", "title": "problem of induction"}, {"id": "08341a63-b759-4c21-a16a-a78a9bd3dbbc", "type": "concept", "title": "uniformity of nature"}, {"id": "a3d3104f-b504-43f0-8789-1264ba7e0b18", "type": "concept", "title": "demonstrative reasoning"}, {"id": "27edafc2-b626-4dc7-b779-f74ae8b707b7", "type": "concept", "title": "probable reasoning"}, {"id": "2540859f-837f-44c4-a6a7-569145961059", "type": "concept", "title": "matter of fact"}, {"id": "2867ef01-7e77-4d0c-a179-57640170a916", "type": "concept", "title": "relations of ideas"}, {"id": "6ef8ec75-7f4b-4cdf-99e9-263bea2ec1a2", "type": "concept", "title": "skeptical argument"}, {"id": "46a432ba-3288-43a2-a716-dbb930c531a4", "type": "concept", "title": "mitigated skepticism"}, {"id": "e6047247-9b3d-4326-b828-9b4c99a47644", "type": "concept", "title": "belief"}, {"id": "e3f5fa68-3fa5-4f20-8545-af4a86624379", "type": "concept", "title": "evidence"}], "description": "Students learn why Hume thinks reason cannot justify expecting the future to resemble the past."}]}, {"id": "399941a8-0f00-44c4-9caf-fe6d8afe2d75", "type": "topic", "title": "Hume: Self, Moral Sentiment, Religion, and Naturalism", "description": "Consider Hume's wider philosophical naturalism in personal identity, ethics, religion, and social life. Evaluate Hume's bundle theory, sentiment-based moral theory, critique of miracles, and naturalistic method.", "children": [{"id": "30616796-f887-4d51-8cbc-8223d872d9e5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "The self and personal identity", "children": [{"id": "b23cb315-87ce-4d78-ad9b-f8fb6a008a7b", "type": "concept", "title": "bundle theory"}, {"id": "68a0a2ce-553c-48a7-b1f3-c8715cf717c6", "type": "concept", "title": "personal identity"}, {"id": "7a44e036-cb83-4b20-a63c-f0de5e332d14", "type": "concept", "title": "perception"}, {"id": "26646975-1d9d-418f-bb10-63e61c45e05e", "type": "concept", "title": "memory"}, {"id": "c768fa45-9a0c-4f1f-864b-3eb93252f7f5", "type": "concept", "title": "fiction"}, {"id": "ad314006-2467-4c12-a883-37befb9af9da", "type": "concept", "title": "imagination"}, {"id": "2318b804-2091-4eed-a4f7-4f25bd202401", "type": "concept", "title": "identity over time"}, {"id": "633f18fc-1c5f-45d6-83ef-1da528f13b2c", "type": "concept", "title": "self"}, {"id": "a551c7bb-0844-47d9-8107-7271ac2bc07b", "type": "concept", "title": "succession"}, {"id": "cb2b6805-a24e-451c-bafd-470f860bfccb", "type": "concept", "title": "theater metaphor"}], "description": "Students analyze Hume's claim that introspection reveals no simple self."}, {"id": "628e7330-3f72-4d6c-bc37-8ac87b427678", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Moral sentiment and motivation", "children": [{"id": "5d192ecf-6ba2-4924-8ccf-8c832f1789f4", "type": "concept", "title": "moral sentiment"}, {"id": "4df0b9f5-bf78-4446-a6ef-bffd58f621ff", "type": "concept", "title": "sympathy"}, {"id": "613fe99a-cdd0-40a0-9c07-c374fb5a0b1a", "type": "concept", "title": "passion"}, {"id": "4218d99b-0c68-4998-bf46-fa0ca507e967", "type": "concept", "title": "reason as slave of the passions"}, {"id": "f26066da-c63d-49b9-9f7b-4ddaaee5a612", "type": "concept", "title": "is-ought problem"}, {"id": "6df367fc-ba54-4cf9-b9a9-9117a348b2a6", "type": "concept", "title": "virtue"}, {"id": "91416a5b-7448-40bc-81c5-201426ed728b", "type": "concept", "title": "vice"}, {"id": "62513850-c4b3-45a1-a2ff-9a1b92675af6", "type": "concept", "title": "utility"}, {"id": "619a6104-7e4a-4f6e-aae1-b8abc3eebe79", "type": "concept", "title": "approval"}, {"id": "4e557ced-ba1b-4ead-865b-c5e8b848c6a2", "type": "concept", "title": "moral psychology"}], "description": "This section develops Hume's challenge to rationalist moral psychology."}, {"id": "f8fd1d04-58f0-40b0-bb96-6ef75bd4b770", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Religion and naturalism", "children": [{"id": "78540aaa-e5f5-44a4-8f14-a061d7ec2608", "type": "concept", "title": "miracle"}, 